    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0525" n="1015" sameAs="frus:frus1948v01p2/pg1015"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.014 Antarctic/11–1948: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in Chile
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d262-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-12-01T19:00:00-05:00">December 1, 1948—7
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>431. Chil Amb Nov 26 handed Daniels<anchor n="2" xml:id="d262-f2"/> draft
                    declaration identical with version Emb London tel Nov 24 rptd Stgo<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d262-f3"/> and requested orally that US Gov join in agreement (Stgo
                    tel 750 Nov 19<anchor n="4" xml:id="d262-f4"/>). Dept expressed to Chil Amb
                    desire to cooperate in every practicable way and to make any confidential or
                    public statement that wld be appropriate in circumstances. On Nov 30 Chil Emb
                    was informed that Dept believes it wld be even more effective and appropriate
                    for US Gov to make a parallel but separate statement either confidentially to
                    three Govs concerned or publicly if those Govs so desired. Basis for separate
                    statement rather than participation in tripartite understanding wld be (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi>) US cld make more unqualified commitment re
                    sending vessels, (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) further Chil negotiation with
                    Arg and Gr Brit wld probably be required for US quadripartite participation, and
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) Dept doubts appropriateness of
                    quadripartite participation because it pertains to problem which has directly
                    concerned only other three countries. Dept’s statement wld be as follows:</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“The Gov of the US is very pleased to learn that the Govs of Arg, Chile and
                        Gr Brit have informed each other that (text of final understanding to be
                        quoted here).</p>
                    <p>This Gov does not contemplate sending any vessels to Antarctic during the
                        1948–1949 Antarctic season”.</p>
                </quote>
                <p>Since US considers not appropriate be party to agreement or declaration, Dept
                    does not feel it shd comment on inclusion of point about no new bases. However,
                    Dept mentioned to Chil Emb our understanding that UK disinclined to include this
                    point.</p>
                <pb facs="0526" n="1016" xml:id="pg1016"/>
                <p>Stgo pls mention foregoing informally to Chil FonMin.</p>
                <p>Rptd to London for informal communication to FonOff and to Buenos Aires for info
                    with requests that Embs obtain informal reaction of UK and Arg Govs to possible
                    US statement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
